      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we should use the @wip annotation here.\n\nYou should make the test as it should be. Theorically it would then fail, but will be skipped if using @wip. Once fixed in a subsequent patch, the test will pass and the @wip will make it to fail, and everything we will need to do is to remove the annotation, the test won\u0027t be touched anymore.\n\nSee [1] and test_get_policy_association at [2] for an example.\n\nThis test would be like:\n\n    @wip(\"reason for marking as wip, etc\")\n    def test_returned_list_size_is_limited(self):\n        self.assertNotEqual(CONF.identity.list_limit, len(default_fixtures.USERS))\n\n        users \u003d self.identity_api.list_users()\n        self.assertEqual(CONF.identity.list_limit, len(users))\n\n[1] https://github.com/openstack/keystone/blob/master/keystone/tests/unit/utils.py#L55\n\n[2] https://review.openstack.org/#/c/212006/6/keystone/tests/unit/backend/endpoint_policy/test_sql.py",
